168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (This course is a basic introduction to Ayurveda and the eight principles that form the framework of Ayurveda dietetics. The Ayurvedic vocabulary to describe the body, mind, and food is explained. Further considerations for personalizing the diet, such as season, quantity, food combinations, and dietary practices, are discussed. At each step, where applicable, a modern nutrition science perspective is provided. Through the examples of pregnancy, iron-deficiency anemia, cognition, and diabetes, integrative dietetics is illustrated. A participatory pedagogy model is adopted so that learning is engaging and participants feel encouraged to apply their knowledge. A 90-page training manual has been developed to complement the lectures.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
